# Everything They Left

A static, single-page story game. The full plan is `RUNBOOK.md`: read it before building anything.

## Stack (do not change)
- Plain HTML + CSS + ES modules. **No frameworks, no bundler, no build step, no new npm packages.**
- three.js r170 from `vendor/three.module.min.js` (import map `"three"`); rough.js from `vendor/rough.js` (global `rough`).
- Serve over http (`python3 -m http.server 8765`); modules don't load from `file://`.
- Reuse `lib/` APIs (stage3d, hud, interactions, notebook, era, archive-map, attempt-map). `prototypes.html` shows
  each one working; copy its patterns. Extend a lib module rather than duplicating it.

## Two workstreams (see HANDOFF.md)
- The game owns `index.html` + `lib/engine.js`. The hangar/pause UI owns `lib/hangar.*` + `hangar.html`.
- They share exactly one file, `lib/progress.js`: the game calls `PROGRESS.unlock(id)`, the hangar renders
  `PROGRESS.entries(CONTENT, missions)` and listens for the `etl:unlock` event. Don't edit the other side's files.
- `content.js`, `data/`, `assets/`, `check.mjs` and the other `lib/*.js` modules are read-only for both.

## Content
- **All story text, facts, interaction configs, waypoints and sources live in `content.js`.** Never hard-code
  story text in HTML/JS. If a line must change, change it in `content.js`.
- Every real-world fact needs a source (a comment in `content.js` and/or the chapter's `sources`). The only fiction
  is Bhoomi, Chandrika Devi, their family, the 2150 storm and the rescue.
- The notebook beat (`CONTENT.notebook`) is shown once, after motivation and before chapter 1, as the first paper card.
- We don't fake the future: anything dated after Sept 2026 must have `projected: true` and a dated `basis`, gets no photo,
  renders as a pencil note tagged PROJECTED. `node check.mjs` enforces this.
- Visual rule: things Bhoomi finds in 2150 are pencil (`<img class="sketch">`, `ensurePencil()`); things she
  relives use `eraFrame(img, year)` — never pick an era look by hand.

## Must keep
- `<meta charset="utf-8">` in every HTML file. `[hidden]{display:none!important}` stays in game.css.
- Keyboard + click alternatives for every interaction (already in lib/interactions.js); the timer switch works
  everywhere; `prefers-reduced-motion` turns off grain/Ken Burns.
- Required credits on the credits screen (see `CREDITS.md`: Solar System Scope CC BY 4.0, Nathan Hughes Hamilton
  CC BY 2.0, ISRO GODL-India, Wikipedia contributors CC BY-SA).

## Known traps (already hit once)
1. SVG timer border: size the viewBox to the element's pixels; never `vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke` with `pathLength`.
2. `display:grid/flex` overrides `[hidden]`.
3. Missing charset turns ’ and — into mojibake.
4. Use CSS animations + `animationend` for timers, not `setInterval`.
5. TDZ: a `const` used before declaration silently kills the module; always read the console.
6. color-dodge order in the pencil filter: `in=blurred negative, in2=grey`.
7. Rotated elements create stacking contexts; `mix-blend-mode` won't reach the page behind them.
8. Browsers cache ES modules; hard-reload after edits.
9. Headless browsers have no WebGL; the stage's still-photo fallback is expected there.
10. Audio plays only after a user gesture (the title hold).

## Direct links (every state must be reachable)
`?screen=title|prologue|opener|map|epilogue|credits` · `?c=air|move|night|library|water|signal&beat=alarm|finds|act|payoff|relive|wonder`
· `&timer=off` · `&misses=N` · `&speed=4` · `&debug=1` (label every element with its name)

## Self-check (run after every change, before showing me anything)
Run `node check.mjs` first: it validates content.js and data/missions.json (missing assets, unknown verbs or icons, wrong counts). Fix anything it lists.
Open each direct link above that the change touches, with `&debug=1`. Read the console first: zero errors.
Screenshot each. Compare with `story.html` (story/content) and `prototypes.html` (components).
List every mismatch as `link · element · expected → actual`. Fix them all, re-check, repeat until the list is empty.
Then show me the screenshots.
